**(a) Thevenin voltage \(V_{\text{th}}\)**  
The two nodes of the bridge are the junctions of \(R_1\!-\!R_2\) and \(R_3\!-\!R_4\).  
The node voltages (with the source \(E=10\;{\rm V}\)) are  

\[
\begin{aligned}
V_a &= E\;\frac{R_2}{R_1+R_2}
     =10\;\frac{1.6\,{\rm k}\Omega}{1\,{\rm k}\Omega+1.6\,{\rm k}\Omega}
     =6.154\;{\rm V} ,\\[4pt]
V_b &= E\;\frac{R_4}{R_3+R_4}
     =10\;\frac{7.5\,{\rm k}\Omega}{3.5\,{\rm k}\Omega+7.5\,{\rm k}\Omega}
     =6.818\;{\rm V} .
\end{aligned}
\]

The Thevenin voltage across the galvanometer terminals is the difference of these node voltages:

\[
V_{\text{th}} = V_a - V_b = 6.154\;{\rm V} - 6.818\;{\rm V}
               = -0.664\;{\rm V}\;\;(\text{magnitude }0.664\;{\rm V}) .
\]

